.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-DEC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-dec
.Nd decapsulate an ML-KEM or HQC shared secret
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis dec
.Fl k Ar key
.Fl o Ar ss | Fl -stdout
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Ar ct
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis dec
recovers the shared secret from the ciphertext
.Ar ct
with the secret KEM key in
.Ar key ,
and writes its 32 bytes to
.Ar ss
(created owner-only, mode 0600) or prints them in hex with
.Fl -stdout .
Exactly one of the two must be given.
.Pp
A ciphertext of the right length that was changed in transit is not an
error: as FIPS 203 and HQC require (implicit rejection), it gives an
unrelated pseudorandom secret and exit status 0.
Whether the secrets agree shows only when they are used, for example when
an authenticated cipher keyed from them fails.
A ciphertext of the wrong length is refused (exit 2).
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl k Ar key , Fl -key Ns = Ns Ar key
A secret KEM key file.
.It Fl o Ar ss , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar ss
The shared-secret file.
.It Fl -stdout
Print the secret in hex instead.
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace an existing
.Ar ss .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success (including implicit rejection); 2 on a usage error, a key that
is not a secret KEM key, a ciphertext of the wrong length, or a file that
cannot be read or written.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis dec -k box -o receiver.ss msg.ct
$ noqtis dec -k box --stdout msg.ct | wc -c
65
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-enc 1 ,
.Xr nqenc 3
